1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,179
How long is your mission?

2
00:00:02,979 --> 00:00:05,028
You've played it, so you have a feeling.

3
00:00:05,478 --> 00:00:06,864
A feeling isn't a number.

4
00:00:08,664 --> 00:00:11,184
Today we measure it with the game's own numbers.

5
00:00:12,084 --> 00:00:13,572
We put a clock on it.

6
00:00:14,472 --> 00:00:17,261
We check by hand that every party can finish.

7
00:00:18,162 --> 00:00:22,322
And we look at what three people are doing in the same minute.

8
00:00:24,122 --> 00:00:25,528
There's one warning first.

9
00:00:25,978 --> 00:00:29,289
A script walked this for us, and a script doesn't read.

10
00:00:30,189 --> 00:00:32,753
So every number today is a floor.

11
00:00:33,953 --> 00:00:36,578
A crew member walks four cells a second.

12
00:00:37,478 --> 00:00:38,821
Your hostiles walk two.

13
00:00:40,621 --> 00:00:43,491
A hostile beside you hits after about two and a half seconds,

14
00:00:43,941 --> 00:00:46,028
and then again every two and a half.

15
00:00:46,928 --> 00:00:48,444
Three hits, and you're down,

16
00:00:48,894 --> 00:00:50,596
in about seven seconds.

17
00:00:52,396 --> 00:00:56,086
If the others are still up, you stay down until somebody brings a medkit.

18
00:00:56,986 --> 00:01:03,373
If everybody's down, you all wake at the entry a few seconds later, with one point each.

19
00:01:05,173 --> 00:01:07,777
And a full shot puts any hostile down in one,

20
00:01:08,227 --> 00:01:09,857
whatever its hit points say.

21
00:01:11,057 --> 00:01:12,474
Now walk your own map.

22
00:01:12,924 --> 00:01:15,074
Count the cells and divide by four.

23
00:01:16,874 --> 00:01:19,806
The landing pad to the way east is seven seconds.

24
00:01:20,706 --> 00:01:24,383
The whole long road, out to the spare cell and back,

25
00:01:24,833 --> 00:01:26,204
is under a minute.

26
00:01:28,004 --> 00:01:30,390
So distance isn't what makes a mission long.

27
00:01:31,290 --> 00:01:34,630
A door on the far side of the map costs your crew seven seconds.

28
00:01:36,430 --> 00:01:39,661
What costs them time is reading, and deciding.

29
00:01:40,111 --> 00:01:41,671
So that's what we count next.

30
00:01:42,871 --> 00:01:45,249
Thirty-one rooms, and nine hundred words.

31
00:01:47,049 --> 00:01:48,818
Three plays, by script.

32
00:01:49,718 --> 00:01:52,612
The long road alone is eleven presses.

33
00:01:53,512 --> 00:01:56,540
With three crew it's still eleven, between them.

34
00:01:58,340 --> 00:02:00,876
And look at this one.

35
00:02:01,326 --> 00:02:05,199
The comms officer, alone, wins in two presses.

36
00:02:06,099 --> 00:02:09,141
Shoot the sentry, take its cell, light the beacon.

37
00:02:09,591 --> 00:02:12,843
That's the starter's design, and it's a kind one.

38
00:02:13,293 --> 00:02:14,122
Just know it's there.

39
00:02:15,922 --> 00:02:18,697
To turn presses into minutes, I have to guess.

40
00:02:19,597 --> 00:02:21,059
Half a minute a press,

41
00:02:21,509 --> 00:02:23,726
and double it for a first play.

42
00:02:24,626 --> 00:02:26,767
Write your own guess beside mine.

43
00:02:27,967 --> 00:02:30,164
You have four ways to press on a crew.

44
00:02:31,064 --> 00:02:32,943
A clock, a patrol,

45
00:02:33,393 --> 00:02:37,436
a key that's somewhere else, and a thing that's hidden.

46
00:02:39,236 --> 00:02:40,564
Here's the clock on the ground,

47
00:02:41,014 --> 00:02:44,571
in the Tasks app, counting down under the starter's quest.

48
00:02:45,471 --> 00:02:49,299
In the file it's one line, and you wrote it in the first class.

49
00:02:50,199 --> 00:02:52,182
Fails when, thirty minutes.

50
00:02:53,982 --> 00:02:56,106
The Lose sentence has to change with it.

51
00:02:56,556 --> 00:02:58,652
It used to say the beacon was slag.

52
00:02:59,552 --> 00:03:02,358
Now it's read when the clock runs out too,

53
00:03:02,808 --> 00:03:05,832
so it has to be true every way.

54
00:03:07,632 --> 00:03:08,738
Then I tell the bridge.

55
00:03:09,188 --> 00:03:11,018
One line in the description,

56
00:03:11,468 --> 00:03:13,333
with an hourglass at the start.

57
00:03:14,233 --> 00:03:15,763
In the Quest Log aboard,

58
00:03:16,213 --> 00:03:19,078
it sits under the quest's first paragraph.

59
00:03:20,878 --> 00:03:23,115
And the clock starts when the quest starts.

60
00:03:23,565 --> 00:03:25,510
This one starts with the game.

61
00:03:26,410 --> 00:03:28,652
So by the time anybody lands,

62
00:03:29,102 --> 00:03:31,229
it already reads a few minutes under thirty.

63
00:03:32,429 --> 00:03:33,726
Lint doesn't walk your map.

64
00:03:34,176 --> 00:03:37,142
You do, on paper, in three lists.

65
00:03:38,942 --> 00:03:41,635
Every area, every item, every ending.

66
00:03:42,085 --> 00:03:44,837
And beside each one, who can do it.

67
00:03:46,637 --> 00:03:49,401
Now find a party the lists leave stuck.

68
00:03:50,301 --> 00:03:53,091
A scientist and a guard, and no engineer.

69
00:03:54,891 --> 00:03:57,344
First she has to reach the terminal alive.

70
00:03:58,244 --> 00:04:00,168
It stands inside the sentry's notice.

71
00:04:01,968 --> 00:04:05,121
So the guard stuns the sentry first,

72
00:04:05,571 --> 00:04:08,031
and she works the terminal while it stands.

73
00:04:08,931 --> 00:04:10,253
Ten seconds isn't long.

74
00:04:10,703 --> 00:04:12,573
If it wakes, stun it again.

75
00:04:13,473 --> 00:04:15,239
Shots miss a lot,

76
00:04:15,689 --> 00:04:18,504
and no app tells you a shot hit or missed.

77
00:04:20,304 --> 00:04:23,318
She pulls the door code, and calms the sentry.

78
00:04:23,768 --> 00:04:25,241
That's the clever answer.

79
00:04:26,141 --> 00:04:27,811
But the sentry keeps its cell,

80
00:04:28,261 --> 00:04:30,498
and nobody here can run the pump.

81
00:04:32,298 --> 00:04:34,395
The clever answer left them with nothing.

82
00:04:35,295 --> 00:04:36,893
So fix it where it broke.

83
00:04:37,343 --> 00:04:39,087
The sentry hands its cell over.

84
00:04:40,887 --> 00:04:44,116
Here's the terminal on the doctor's handheld after the update.

85
00:04:45,016 --> 00:04:47,016
The words say the sentry walks over.

86
00:04:47,466 --> 00:04:50,463
On the map it just stands where the stun caught it.

87
00:04:51,363 --> 00:04:53,176
And there's the power cell in her pack.

88
00:04:54,076 --> 00:04:57,203
In the file it's one outcome, after a comma.

89
00:04:58,403 --> 00:05:00,638
Three columns, one for each console.

90
00:05:01,088 --> 00:05:03,436
What is each person doing?

91
00:05:05,236 --> 00:05:07,093
This is the mission as you left it.

92
00:05:07,993 --> 00:05:10,350
The chief makes eight presses out of twelve.

93
00:05:10,800 --> 00:05:13,294
The doctor is finished in ten seconds.

94
00:05:15,094 --> 00:05:16,502
What you have there is a chain.

95
00:05:16,952 --> 00:05:19,017
Every step waits for the one before,

96
00:05:19,467 --> 00:05:22,147
so only one person is ever busy.

97
00:05:23,947 --> 00:05:26,001
The cure is a join.

98
00:05:26,451 --> 00:05:30,210
Make the thing in the middle need pieces from three places.

99
00:05:32,010 --> 00:05:34,097
Your pump needs three fuses.

100
00:05:34,547 --> 00:05:37,203
So give Marrow one to pay the doctor with.

101
00:05:38,103 --> 00:05:41,659
On her handheld, he pays with the fuse out of his kettle,

102
00:05:42,109 --> 00:05:43,558
and it's in her pack.

103
00:05:44,458 --> 00:05:47,834
In the file, it's one more outcome on the cough answer.

104
00:05:49,634 --> 00:05:52,800
Now three people each carry something to the pump house,

105
00:05:53,250 --> 00:05:55,618
and nobody presses more than five times.

106
00:05:56,818 --> 00:05:58,660
Put it together in a beat sheet.

107
00:05:59,560 --> 00:06:01,564
One column is the stand-in's clock,

108
00:06:02,014 --> 00:06:03,214
and that one is measured.

109
00:06:04,114 --> 00:06:05,898
The other is my guess for a first play.

110
00:06:07,698 --> 00:06:09,400
Now play it with a stopwatch,

111
00:06:09,850 --> 00:06:12,462
and write your own times over mine.

112
00:06:14,262 --> 00:06:16,931
For forty-five minutes, write the sheet first.

113
00:06:17,831 --> 00:06:19,434
Five for the landing.

114
00:06:19,884 --> 00:06:21,747
Twenty for three tracks.

115
00:06:22,197 --> 00:06:23,609
Eight for the join.

116
00:06:24,509 --> 00:06:26,245
Seven for the last area,

117
00:06:26,695 --> 00:06:29,806
and five for the ending.

118
00:06:31,606 --> 00:06:33,857
That sheet is where your own mission starts.
